# Installation-scoped runtime state, secrets, OAuth caches (KTD21).
# Nothing in here is ever committed. Library-scoped state does not live in the
# repository at all; it lives beside the library, so it needs no rule here.
.local/

# The tree registry describes one person's library and their cutover flips
# (KTD22). Committing it would ship those flips to every friend.
tree_registry.json

# Per-clone list of a contributor's own drive, account, and machine names, read
# by scripts/scan_repo.py so it can catch those names written WITHOUT a path
# around them (R1). It is the one file in the repository that deliberately names
# a specific person, so it is the one file that must never be committed. See
# .scan-identity.example for the format.
.scan-identity

# Python build / install artifacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
*.egg
build/
dist/
.eggs/

# Virtualenvs. No trailing slash: a slash matches a DIRECTORY only, and a
# .venv SYMLINK slipped past the slashed pattern and was committed pointing at
# an absolute path on one machine. scripts/scan_repo.py now catches that shape
# too, so this is the first of two independent defences rather than the only one.
.venv
venv
env/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Editor / tooling
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Test / type-check caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Raw idea capture, private scratch (planning convention)
docs/backlog.md

# Agent worktrees
.claude/worktrees/
.worktrees/
